# Generated from: specs/591-record-bdd-as-the-only-kept-test-layer-and-convert-the-doc-contract-tests-into-bdd-scenarios/requirements.md
Feature: Record bdd as the only kept test layer and convert the doc contract tests into BDD scenarios

  @SCN001
  Scenario: The repository keeps bdd as its only test type
    Given the approved upgrade plan
    When the test-layers item is applied with --kept bdd
    Then steering/test-layers.json is {"version":1,"kept":["bdd"]}

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The contribution gate workflow matches its managed contract
    Given the shared contribution-gate reference and the dogfooded workflow
    When the contract is read
    Then the managed version, lifecycle status, collision rules and minimal permissions are documented
    And the dogfooded workflow equals the canonical embedded template

  @SCN003
  Scenario: The contribution guide uses v4 invocations
    Given the shared contribution-guide reference
    When it is read
    Then it uses v4 /sdlc-* invocations and specs/{N}-{slug} paths

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Interactive commands use native plan mode
    Given the interactive workflows and the hooks module
    When their contract is read
    Then plan entry, AskUserQuestion and ExitPlanMode are documented and no plugin bypass is referenced

  @SCN005
  Scenario: The managed GitHub issue form is valid and referenced
    Given .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/nmg-sdlc-ready-issue.yml
    When it is parsed
    Then its required fields, ids, labels and dropdown options are present, unique and schema-safe
    And onboarding, upgrade-project, README and CHANGELOG reference it

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Onboarding creates the changelog
    Given the onboard-project workflow
    When each onboarding path is read
    Then it creates CHANGELOG.md with an [Unreleased] heading

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Onboarding creates the stage models file
    Given the onboard-project workflow
    When an approved onboarding plan is read
    Then it runs sdlc-models.mjs ensure, and already-initialized onboarding recommends upgrade instead

  @SCN008
  Scenario: The README documents per-project stage models
    Given README.md
    When its models sections are read
    Then they describe steering/sdlc-models.json, its defaults, its diagnostics and its upgrade path

  @SCN009
  Scenario: The simplify workflow is bundled only into implementation
    Given workflows/simplify/WORKFLOW.md
    When the plugin bundles workflows
    Then only the implementation surface includes it

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Spec context stays bounded
    Given the spec-context and project-agents references
    When they are read
    Then they use specs/{N}-{slug} with Related Spec neighbors and keep the managed markers

  @SCN011
  Scenario: Start-issue requires an explicit issue
    Given the start-issue workflow
    When it is read
    Then it requires an explicit issue number, treats an epic label as ordinary and keeps the compact controller invocation

  @SCN012
  Scenario: The status workflow keeps its compact contract
    Given workflows/status/WORKFLOW.md and scripts/sdlc-status.mjs
    When they are read
    Then the workflow uses name and description frontmatter only and leaves recommendations to the script

  @SCN013
  Scenario: Repository steering describes the Claude Code plugin
    Given the steering snippets and plugin manifest
    When they are read
    Then they use the Claude Code plugin identity, declare every version mirror and contain no unresolved placeholders

  @SCN014
  Scenario: Upgrade documents the v4 host-language migration
    Given the upgrade-project workflow and references
    When they are read
    Then they name all three upgrade groups and their fail-closed reason codes
    And this repository uses CLAUDE.md

  @SCN015
  Scenario: CI rejects a test of a type the project does not keep
    Given steering/test-layers.json keeps bdd only
    And a unit or doc test file that the allowlist does not list
    When node scripts/check-test-layers.mjs --root . runs
    Then it exits 1 with test_layers_type_not_kept naming the file and its type

  @SCN016
  Scenario: The allowlist only shrinks
    Given scripts/test-layers-allowlist.json lists a file that is missing or now a bdd test
    When the check runs
    Then it exits 1 with test_layers_allowlist_stale
    And an invalid steering/test-layers.json exits 1 with test_layers_invalid

  @SCN017
  Scenario: CI runs the kept-layer check before the tests
    Given .github/workflows/nmg-sdlc-verify.yml
    When the verify job runs
    Then node scripts/check-test-layers.mjs --root . runs before the Jest suite
